          "id": "commentary_3_1-guidance-1",
          "type": "commentary_guidance",
          "text": "To achieve a mark in Level 3, students must give details of both reagents and both positive results, as well as at least one risk with its linked control measure. In addition, students must include good scientific terminology \u2013 as such, we would expect Level 3 students to be clear in their wording, e.g. iodine solution (which could be inferred by using \u2018drops\u2019) in the starch test, and in the Benedict\u2019s test they should convey a clear understanding of the need to heat the mixture appropriately. ",
          "order": 1,
          "parent_id": null,
